values ('bbbb0005-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 'en', null, 'Portuguese & Brazilian Culture', 'A tour of the Lusophone world - Portugal, Brazil, and Portuguese-speaking Africa - across its history, language, literature, music, art, food, and faith. The structure and reference facts are adapted from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0), with all prose written originally for this course. By the end you can trace how one language came to link roughly 260 million people on four continents.', null, 'foundations', 43, true, 'humanities', '{}')
